               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Severe aortic stenosis, TAVI or surgical valve replacement performed</div>
               </text>
            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding the discharge of your 80-year-old female patient admitted with severe aortic valve stenosis. Following admission, comprehensive diagnostic workup was performed including echocardiography confirming severe aortic stenosis with significantly reduced valve area and elevated mean pressure gradient. Coronary angiography was performed to exclude significant coronary artery disease prior to intervention. Given her age and surgical risk profile, the interdisciplinary heart team consensus favoured transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI) over surgical replacement. The procedure was performed successfully via transfemoral access without significant complications. Post-procedural echocardiography demonstrated excellent valve function with markedly improved haemodynamics. The patient recovered well and remained haemodynamically stable throughout her stay. Please continue antiplatelet therapy as prescribed and arrange follow-up echocardiography in three months. Do not hesitate to contact us should any concerns arise.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
